.env
**/.env
# Every dotenv sibling, not just `.env` itself. haven writes `.env.portless`
# into the worktree and server.mts loads it with override:true at boot, so a
# copy of it inside the build context would bake a dev stack's overrides —
# retention default, admin password, access tokens — into the image and let
# them win over whatever the deployment configured.
.env.*
**/.env.*
# `.env.example` is tracked documentation with no secrets in it.
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
**/.venv

